# generic_union_arg.tkr — the §9.D CR2 ACCEPT host: a GENERIC struct instantiated with an INLINE UNION
# type-argument (`Parsed<@ValA()>`), the shape that blocked retiring `Pattern`. The checker's
# `type_mangle` collapsed every inline union to the nameless stamp `variant`, so a value read back off
# the generic's `T`-typed field lost the union's members (widening/type-eq failed) and two distinct
# unions shared one `Parsed__g__variant` instance. Encoding the members in the mangle fixes both. Each
# scenario names itself and asserts its announced value through `run` in `main.tks`. Inert on the seed:
# no generic in `src/` is instantiated with an inline union yet — this is the additive checker fix.

Feature: generic_union_arg — §9.D CR2 generic over an inline-union type-argument

  Scenario: field_readback — a T-typed `node` read off Parsed<@ValA()> widens into a direct union field (Leaf → 1)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario field_readback: ok"

  Scenario: slice_readback — a T-typed `node` pushed into a directly-typed []@ValA() matches the element type (→ 1)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario slice_readback: ok"

  Scenario: distinct_insts — Parsed<@ValA()> and Parsed<@ValB()> are DISTINCT instances, not collided to __g__variant (1*10+1 → 11)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario distinct_insts: ok"
